    "https://www.colorado.edu/jobs/benefits": {
      "title": "Benefits",
      "description": "Benefits | CU Boulder Jobs | University of Colorado Boulder Skip to main content CU Boulder Jobs Home Living Here Benefits Perks Search Jobs Translate English Spanish Chinese French German Korean Lao Nepali Japanese Tibetan Search Enter the terms you wish to search for. Other ways to search: Events Calendar Campus Map CU Boulder Jobs Home Living Here Benefits Perks Search Jobs Search for CU Anschutz, Denver, Colorado Springs or System Jobs FAQ Human Resources Benefits Benefits Your total compensation extends far beyond your pay—that’s why we’ve put together an unparalleled benefits package for you. Based on the details of your position, you may be eligible for: Compare Medical Plans Medical Plans At CU we take care of our own. That's why the CU system covers 85 to 90 percent of your medical premiums. With four different healthcare plans to choose from, we offer the flexibility to find a plan that works for you. More About Medical Plans Compare Medical Plans Dental and Vision Plans CU Boulder offers two different dental plans to choose from for all your dental needs, and a vision plan that ensures that your family is covered. More About Dental Plans More About Vision Plans Paid Parental Leave If eligible, Paid Parental leave grants you 240 hours (6 weeks) of paid leave to be taken within one year of the birth, adoption, foster placement or guardianship of a child. More About Paid Parental Leave Life Insurance We offer a full suite basic life insurance, optional life insurance and voluntary accidental death & dismemberment insurance policies. Learn More About Life Insurance Pre-tax Savings Plans We offer Health Care Flexible Spending Accounts (HCFSA), Health Savings Accounts (HSA) and Dependent Care Flexible Savings Accounts. We've got you covered! Learn More About Pre-tax Savings Plans Retirement Eligible employees are automatically enrolled in a generous savings plan that will help them get ready to enjoy retirement, comfortably. If that’s not enough, we also offer several voluntary savings options from which to choose. Learn More About Retirement Savings Tuition Benefit At CU Boulder we value progression, education and growth. That’s why we offer tuition benefits for all eligible employees. Learn More About the Tuition Benefit Leave Benefits Here at CU, we understand that life happens. Whether you’re planning a vacation or in need of personal or family medical leave, we offer a variety of leave options. View Our Holiday Schedule Learn More About Leave Benefits Faculty & Staff Assistance Program Trained general counselors are dedicated to serving the emotional and psychological needs of the campus community. All CU Boulder faculty and staff are eligible to meet with an FSAP counselor. Learn More About FSAP CU Boulder Jobs Submit a Request for Help Frequently Asked Questions For Technical Support: 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) The University of Colorado does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, age, pregnancy, disability, creed, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, marital status, political affiliation, or political philosophy. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. You may view the list of ADA and Title IX coordinators and review the Regent policy . This organization participates in E-Verify . We will provide the Social Security Administration and, if necessary, the Department of Homeland Security, with information from each employee's I-9 form to confirm work authorization. Reasonable Accommodations for Applicants with Disabilities CU Boulder is committed to making information and resources that are available via the web accessible for all users. If you are a job seeker and need accessibility assistance or an accommodation in order to apply for one of our open positions, please submit an accessibility request or call 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) to submit a request for assistance. Download the Clery Act Annual Security & Fire safety report , or request a paper copy from the CU Boulder Police Department . Administrative and Research Center, East Campus • 3100 Marine St. • Boulder, CO 80309-0565 University of Colorado Boulder © Regents of the University of Colorado Privacy • Legal & Trademarks • Campus Map University of Colorado Boulder © Regents of the University of Colorado"
    },
    "https://www.colorado.edu/jobs/perks": {
      "title": "Perks",
      "description": "Perks | CU Boulder Jobs | University of Colorado Boulder Skip to main content CU Boulder Jobs Home Living Here Benefits Perks Search Jobs Translate English Spanish Chinese French German Korean Lao Nepali Japanese Tibetan Search Enter the terms you wish to search for. Other ways to search: Events Calendar Campus Map CU Boulder Jobs Home Living Here Benefits Perks Search Jobs Search for CU Anschutz, Denver, Colorado Springs or System Jobs FAQ Human Resources Perks Perks We know that you work hard. That's why we’ve put together these awesome perks to help you make the most of your time off. Search for Jobs Child and Elder Care Bright Horizons CU Boulder has partnered with Bright Horizons to help employees better manage work, family, and personal responsibilities. There are two programs available to eligible employees: Back-Up Child, Adult, and Elder Care Enhanced Family Supports CU Children's Center The CU Children’s Center prioritizes children of CU Boulder graduate and undergraduate students, faculty, staff and alumni. Other Childcare Discounts ​ As a state employer, CU Boulder employees are eligible to participate in the State of Colorado’s employee discount program. Counseling, Support and Wellness Faculty and Staff Assistance Program Dedicated to serving the emotional and psychological needs of the campus community. FSAP offers free teletherapy and in-person (including outdoors) counseling to CU Boulder faculty and staff. Wellness Events Free Workshops and seminars for wellness and work-life. Topics range from gardening to mindfulness to nutrition. Self-Paced/ On-Demand Support App based support for those that need it. Discount Programs BenefitHub As a state employer, CU Boulder employees are eligible to participate in the State of Colorado’s employee discount program. EcoPass Extra Program Use the EcoPass and save with discounts at restaurants, stores and more! Just flash the EcoPass at participating local businesses. CU Athletics Discounts Eligible CU Boulder employees may receive discounts on CU Buffs season tickets and some single game tickets when offered. CU Presents Discounts CU Presents offers all CU Boulder faculty and staff with valid Buff One cards a discount on all Artist Series, Eklund Opera, and some special events! Learning & Development Tuition Assistance Benefit Eligible employees may receive nine (9) waived credits for eligible courses at any CU campus per academic year, or in any given academic year, running from fall to summer, an eligible employee may give their Tuition Assistance Benefit to an eligible dependent or split it between multiple dependents. Employee Learning & Professional Development Organization & Employee Development offers a comprehensive learning catalog to CU Boulder employees. CU Employee Leadership & Management Certificate The University of Colorado Department of Human Resources (HR) and the Lockheed Martin Engineering Management Program (EMP) have partnered to offer a graduate Leadership and Management certificate for CU employees. On-Demand Learning with Linkedin and CU on Coursera Fitness & Nutrition Fitness Center Discounts & Weightloss Programs (Sponsored by Be Colorado) All employees at the University of Colorado (CU) and CU Medicine (CUMed) are eligible for these great discounts at a variety of gyms and fitness centers along the Front Range. CU Recreation Center Faculty or staff employed on the Boulder campus, Boulder campus retirees, and employees of University System offices in Boulder are eligible for a membership to the CU Boulder Recreation Center. Be Colorado for CU Health Plan Members CU Health Plan and Be Colorado have teamed up to provide employees with a full spectrum of programs. These programs are designed to give employees with CU Health plans the information, inspiration and support needed to achieve their best self. Hiking & Outdoors Explore 300 miles of captivating trails, 45,000 acres of unspoiled open space or the Boulder Creek Path, which runs through the middle of town. Check out what Boulder offers those wanting to get outdoors. Financial TIAA One-on-One Financial Consultation CU employees are eligible to meet with financial professionals from the university’s retirement plan service provider Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association of America (TIAA) at no cost. Discuss any financial issue—from everyday budgeting to managing debt and (of course) retirement planning. Public Service Loan Forgiveness CU is a 501(c)(3) not-for-profit qualifying employer under the PSLF program. Employee Services, the CU System office that serves all four campuses, will assist you in completing Public Service Loan Forgiveness form. Transportation Eco-Pass CU Boulder provides passes for qualifying employees. The passes provide access to all Local, Limited, Express and Regional bus service, in all fare zones, including the SkyRide bus service to DIA*. (*Not valid on special services, including but not limited to Access‑a‑Ride, BroncosRide, BuffRide, RockiesRide, RunRide, Saturday Shopper, and SeniorRide.) B-cycle cycle bike sharing provides an opportunity for convenient, cost-effective, and eco-friendly transportation around Boulder.  There are 280 bikes at 40 stations around Boulder and 10 stations serving the CU Boulder campus. CU Boulder employees can purchase an unlimited pass at a discounted rate. UMC and Folsom Bike Stations The CU bike station mechanics are here to assist you in maintaining your registered bike and in doing light repairs. CU Boulder Jobs Submit a Request for Help Frequently Asked Questions For Technical Support: 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) The University of Colorado does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, age, pregnancy, disability, creed, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, marital status, political affiliation, or political philosophy. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. You may view the list of ADA and Title IX coordinators and review the Regent policy . This organization participates in E-Verify . We will provide the Social Security Administration and, if necessary, the Department of Homeland Security, with information from each employee's I-9 form to confirm work authorization. Reasonable Accommodations for Applicants with Disabilities CU Boulder is committed to making information and resources that are available via the web accessible for all users. If you are a job seeker and need accessibility assistance or an accommodation in order to apply for one of our open positions, please submit an accessibility request or call 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) to submit a request for assistance. Download the Clery Act Annual Security & Fire safety report , or request a paper copy from the CU Boulder Police Department . Administrative and Research Center, East Campus • 3100 Marine St. • Boulder, CO 80309-0565 University of Colorado Boulder © Regents of the University of Colorado Privacy • Legal & Trademarks • Campus Map University of Colorado Boulder © Regents of the University of Colorado"
    },
