    "https://www.colorado.edu/jobs/frequently-asked-questions": {
      "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
      "description": "Frequently Asked Questions | CU Boulder Jobs | University of Colorado Boulder Skip to main content CU Boulder Jobs Home Living Here Benefits Perks Search Jobs Translate English Spanish Chinese French German Korean Lao Nepali Japanese Tibetan Search Enter the terms you wish to search for. Other ways to search: Events Calendar Campus Map CU Boulder Jobs Home Living Here Benefits Perks Search Jobs Search for CU Anschutz, Denver, Colorado Springs or System Jobs FAQ Human Resources Frequently Asked Questions Applying For a Job Who can I contact for information about the job posting? Please contact the \"Job Posting Contact\" listed in the job ad with any questions about the posting. I previously created an account with CU Careers. Can I use those same credentials to log in to the CU Boulder Jobs site? CU Careers is the job site for the other University of Colorado campuses and is not affiliated with the Boulder campus job site, CU Boulder Jobs. The log-ins are not transferable. To apply to a job at CU Boulder, please register a new account on the CU Boulder Jobs site by applying for a job, registering for the talent community , or by creating a Job Alert . Note: Current CU Boulder employees, with the exception of student employees, automatically have a profile on the CU Boulder Internal Jobs site and should not register an additional account through the external job site. If you are a former CU employee and are experiencing technical difficulties logging in, reach out to recruiting@colorado.edu for assistance. Former employees who worked at CU Boulder prior to May 2017 will need to create a new account. How do I register for an account on the CU Boulder Jobs Site? You can create an account by applying for a job , registering for the talent community , or by creating a Job Alert . Note: CU Boulder employees automatically have a profile on the CU Boulder Internal Jobs site and should not register an additional account through the external job site. Can I save my application and come back to it later? If you exit the application before finalizing the last step in your submission, you will have the ability to complete your application later, as long as the job is still active on our career site. To complete an in-progress application, go to your \"My Profile\" page in the \"Jobs I Have Applied To\" section and click the “Complete Application” button. How do I know if my application was received? You will receive an email from CU Boulder Jobs confirming the successful submission of your application. Additionally, you can view a list of your active job applications from your \"My Profile Page\" in the \"Jobs I Have Applied To\" section. Note: if you receive this email, it means we have received all the required application documents. How do I check my application status? You can check the status of your application from the “Jobs I Have Applied To” section of your “My Profile” page. How do I update my application materials? You can edit your profile information (work and education history) at any time from the “My Profile” page. If you have already submitted your application and need to update your documents (e.g. resume or cover letter), please contact the \"Job Posting Contact\" listed for the position to which you have applied. If you are unable to locate this information, contact us at recruiting@colorado.edu . Please do not withdraw your application as you will not be able to re-apply with updated materials. I forgot my password. How do I log back into my profile? You can reset your password by using the “Forgot your Password” feature from the login page. If you have an existing account with CU Boulder Jobs, you'll be sent an email with instructions on how to reset your password. If you have trouble resetting your password you can email recruiting@colorado.edu . Please do not create a new profile. Note: Internal CU Boulder employees must log in through the Internal CU Boulder Jobs site and will be prompted to log in using IdentiKey credentials. How do I update/change my existing password? After logging into your account, you can update your password by clicking the “Reset Password” button in the Account Management section of your “My Profile” page. You will be asked to confirm your email address and will then receive an email with instructions for how to change your password. Note: Internal CU Boulder employees must log in through the Internal CU Boulder Jobs site and will be prompted to log in using IdentiKey credentials. What if I would like to update the email address associated with my account? To change the email address associated with your account, log in to the career site and navigate to 'My Profile'. Select 'Update Profile' to edit your email address. This action will update the email address used to log in and all subsequent application notifications will be sent to this email account. Note: If you are a former CU Boulder employee experiencing technical difficulties updating your email, contact recruiting@colorado.edu for assistance. Search For Jobs I want to work at CU Boulder. How do I find out what vacancies are available? Please visit the CU Boulder Jobs site for the most current list of job openings. You can filter the list by area of interest, functional area, posting title, or posting number. You can also create a Job Alert to be automatically notified of new postings that meet your specific criteria. What is a Job Alert? You can create a Job Alert to be automatically notified of new postings that meet your specific criteria. Once a job alert is created, you can edit or remove the job alerts from within the \"My Profile\" page of your account. To ensure job alerts don't land in your spam folder, add 'CU Boulder Jobs < no-reply@colorado.edu>' to your contacts or trusted senders list. How do I modify or stop receiving Job Alerts? You can modify or delete your Job Alert at any time from the “My Profile” page of your account. To ensure job alerts don't land in your spam folder, add 'CU Boulder Jobs < no-reply@colorado.edu>' to your contacts or trusted senders list. I am a current CU Boulder employee. How do I search/apply for jobs? If you are a current CU Boulder employee, please visit the Internal CU Boulder Jobs site to search or apply for staff, faculty or research faculty jobs. You will be prompted to log in using your IdentiKey credentials. Please do not register a new account on the external CU Boulder Jobs site as this may result in an error when submitting applications. I am a CU retiree. How do I search/apply for jobs? Retirees interested in work will need to submit their information to our applicant tracking system, as we will be keeping all information in our Avature retiree talent community moving forward. Please email recruiting@colorado.edu for more information and assistance. I entered my search criteria, but am not seeing related results. How do I find jobs that meet my criteria? It's possible that there are no matching jobs to meet your criteria at the moment. Please check back soon or create a Job Alert to be notified of new postings that meet your criteria. How long will the posting be available? Applications will be accepted through 11:59 pm Mountain Standard Time of the Posting Close Date listed in the job posting details. Please refer to the special instructions section in the posting for additional requirements regarding application deadlines or full consideration dates. I no longer see a previously posted job. Can I still apply? CU Boulder Jobs contains the most up to date list of available postings. If you do not see a position posted on our site, we are no longer accepting applications. Please note that our jobs are shared with or otherwise collected by various outside job boards. These outside job boards will direct you to apply at CU Boulder Jobs , however their job posting list may not be updated as frequently as the list on our site. I don’t see a vacancy I'm interested in at the moment. How can I stay in touch? You can create a Job Alert to receive notifications of new postings that meet your specific criteria. We also encourage you to register for our talent community to receive exclusive updates about new job opportunities or upcoming events. CU Boulder Talent Community What is the CU Boulder Talent Community? The CU Boulder Talent Community is an opt-in monthly email newsletter. It shares news and highlights about CU Boulder and includes a sampling of featured job opportunities. To ensure the Talent Community Newsletter doesn't land in your spam folder, add 'CU Boulder Jobs < no-reply@colorado.edu>' to your contacts or trusted senders list. How do I join the CU Boulder Talent Community? To join the CU Boulder Talent Community , submit the required information and specify an area of interest. I created a profile in the CU Boulder Talent Community. Does that mean I've applied? No, the talent community allows you to express interest in CU Boulder and receive exclusive updates on new opportunities and upcoming events. You must apply to a job in order to be considered for a specific position. References When will I be asked to provide references? Though not required at the time of application, finalists for staff positions will be contacted to provide professional references. Please refer to the 'special instructions' section in the job posting, which may outline additional details about the position's requirements. When will I be requested to submit letter providers for letters of recommendation? Letters of recommendation are typically collected for faculty and research faculty positions. If letters of recommendation are required, the request for letter provider names may happen either at the time of application or later in the process. You will be contacted directly via email with additional details if letter providers are required after application. I need to change or edit one of my confidential letter reference providers. What do I do? You can edit your letter providers for a specific job application from the \"My Profile\" page in the CU Boulder Jobs portal . To do so, log into your account, and from the “Jobs I Have Applied To” list, select “Manage References”. From this page, select \"Edit References\" to modify the letter providers submitted for that position. Once the request for letters has been initiated, you cannot edit the contact information for your letter providers. However, you can add additional letter providers by selecting \"Manage References\" then “Add References” from the “Jobs I Have Applied To” list on the “My Profile” page. My letter provider did not receive a request for a recommendation or is unable to upload their letter. What do I do? HR can resend the request to the letter provider on your behalf and can provide support. Please contact us with the title of the position and name/email of your letter provider and we will follow up with them. You should have received an email from one of our recruitment coordinators earlier in the search process and can send this information directly to that person. If you did not receive an email or are unsure who your recruitment coordinator is, please contact us at recruiting@colorado.edu .​ How and when will my letter provider be notified to submit a confidential letter of recommendation? Your letter provider(s) will receive an email with instructions and a URL for submitting the confidential letter of recommendation. The letter(s) of recommendation may be collected at any time throughout the search process. As the candidate, you will also receive an email notifying you when we have initiated the collection of letter(s) of recommendation.​ My letter provider does not want to submit an online response. Can a paper letter be sent in? Letters of recommendation must be submitted online. Contact your assigned recruitment coordinator if you need support. If you did not receive an email or are unsure who your recruitment coordinator is, please contact us at recruiting@colorado.edu . How do I know if letters of recommendation have been submitted? If we are at a point in the search process where we want to proceed with your application and have not received the required letter(s) of recommendation, we will contact you to ask for your assistance with following up with your letter provider(s). You can verify or monitor the status of letters of recommendation from the \"My Profile\" page in the CU Boulder Jobs portal . To do so, log into your account, and from the “Jobs I Have Applied To” list, select “Manage References”. If you have any questions about the letters of recommendation process or the status of submissions for your application, you can contact your recruitment coordinator (Note: please include the job posting title and number and any other relevant details in the email so that we can best assist you). If you are unsure who your recruitment coordinator is, please contact us at recruiting@colorado.edu .​ Additional Information Will my position require me to work in person, or will it be fully remote? This depends on the nature of work being performed, the size of the work unit, and campus needs. Positions on our campus may be entirely remote, in-person or a hybrid of both. Work modality may change over time depending on a variety of factors. To the extent possible, we will note the work modality on job postings. I notice many job postings have a salary range listed; how is the exact salary determined for a new hire? The salary of the finalist selected for this role will be set based on a variety of job-related factors, including but not limited to internal equity, experience, education, licensure/certification if applicable, specialty, and training. What internet browsers are compatible with the CU Boulder Jobs career site? The CU Boulder Jobs career site supports all current major browsers and platforms. If you're experiencing issues, double-check that your browser and all platforms are up to date. Didn't Find What You Were Looking For? Didn't find what you were looking for? For technical issues, please submit a request for help or contact Talent Acquisition at recruiting@colorado.edu with any questions. CU Boulder Jobs Submit a Request for Help Frequently Asked Questions For Technical Support: 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) The University of Colorado does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, age, pregnancy, disability, creed, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, marital status, political affiliation, or political philosophy. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. You may view the list of ADA and Title IX coordinators and review the Regent policy . This organization participates in E-Verify . We will provide the Social Security Administration and, if necessary, the Department of Homeland Security, with information from each employee's I-9 form to confirm work authorization. Reasonable Accommodations for Applicants with Disabilities CU Boulder is committed to making information and resources that are available via the web accessible for all users. If you are a job seeker and need accessibility assistance or an accommodation in order to apply for one of our open positions, please submit an accessibility request or call 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) to submit a request for assistance. Download the Clery Act Annual Security & Fire safety report , or request a paper copy from the CU Boulder Police Department . Administrative and Research Center, East Campus • 3100 Marine St. • Boulder, CO 80309-0565 University of Colorado Boulder © Regents of the University of Colorado Privacy • Legal & Trademarks • Campus Map University of Colorado Boulder © Regents of the University of Colorado"
    },
    "https://jobs.colorado.edu/jobs/Login": {
      "title": "JobsUNIVERSITY OF COLORADOBOULDER",
