    "https://jobs.colorado.edu/jobs/JobDetail/Assistant-Associate-Professor-of-Organizational-Behavior/74535": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Organizational Behavior",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Organizational Behavior Jobs UNIVERSITY OF COLORADO BOULDER Jobs UNIVERSITY OF COLORADO BOULDER Skip to content Search jobs Living Here Benefits Perks Jobs Join the CU Boulder Talent Community Create Job Alert FAQ Login Join the CU Boulder Talent Community Create Job Alert FAQ Login Home Job Detail Assistant/Associate Professor of Organizational Behavior Requisition Number: 74535 Location: Boulder, Colorado City Boulder State Colorado Employment Type: Faculty Schedule: Full-Time Date Posted: 28-Aug-2026 Close All Job Summary The Leeds School of Business at the University of Colorado Boulder is hiring an Assistant/Associate Professor of Organizational Behavior position in Organizational Leadership and Information Analytics (OLIA) Division, starting in Fall 2027. We are seeking candidates with recent success or a strong potential in publishing high-quality and impactful research in leading management journals. A successful candidate should exhibit a strong willingness and ability to teach courses in organizational behavior and management, as well as a strong willingness and ability to effectively interact with faculty colleagues, students, staff, and external constituents. We are interested in candidates with a grounding in Organizational Behavior or an allied discipline who are pursuing work in the area of Organizational Behavior. CU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and complies with all applicable federal, state, and local laws governing nondiscrimination in employment. We are committed to creating a workplace where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity, and we encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply, including protected veterans and individuals with disabilities. Who We Are The University of Colorado Boulder, and the city of Boulder, offer a rich intellectual, cultural, recreational, and family-friendly environment. The economy of the Front Range of Colorado is strong, and private support for the University and the Leeds School is increasing steadily, as evidenced by our new programs and solid MBA program. The University of Colorado and the Leeds School of Business are nationally recognized for the excellence of our faculty, programs, and students. By joining Leeds, you will become part of a collegial and productive group of Organizational Behavior scholars committed to research and teaching excellence. Our faculty actively publish and serve on the editorial boards of leading management journals, including but not limited to the Academy of Management Journal, Academy of Management Review, Organization Science, Journal of Applied Psychology, and Organizational Behavior and Human Decision Processes. Our faculty are also passionate about conducting research that has a meaningful societal or practical impact. Boulder is a satellite community of about 107,000 people with excellent schools located 30 minutes from downtown Denver, a few hours from world-renown ski resorts, at the heart of the Colorado startup ecosystem, and has over 300 sunny days each year. The Boulder/Denver area is one of the fastest growing regions in America, has a metropolitan population of about 3.4 million, and is surrounded by stunning scenery. The University of Colorado also offers an excellent early childhood and preschool education facility attended by students who collectively speak over 50 languages. What Your Key Responsibilities Will Be Minimum qualifications include a doctorate in Organizational Behavior or an allied discipline (e.g., Human Resources, Psychology, Labor and Employment Relations / Industrial Relations), a strong willingness and ability to teach courses in organizational behavior and management, and the demonstrated ability to conduct high-quality and impactful (quantitative and/or qualitative) academic research. Candidates who are Ph.D. students must be close to completion of their Ph.D. degrees (all completed but Ph.D. dissertation). The Ph.D. degree should be obtained before the appointment starts. What We Can Offer The salary range for an Assistant Professor ($190,000–$200,000) or Associate Professor ($215,000–$230,000). Additional benefits include allowance with relocation expenses and for a computer, FDA (Faculty Development Account), and a specific amount of guaranteed summer research support. Benefits At the University of Colorado Boulder , we are committed to supporting the holistic health and well-being of our employees. Our comprehensive benefits package includes medical, dental, and retirement plans; generous paid time off; tuition assistance for you and your dependents; and an ECO Pass for local transit. As one of Boulder County’s largest employers, CU Boulder offers an inspiring academic community and access to world-class outdoor recreation. Explore additional perks and programs through the CU Advantage program. Be Statements Be creative. Be impactful. Be Boulder. What We Require Candidates must hold a Ph.D. degree or equivalent in Organizational Behavior or a closely related field or be close to completion of a Ph.D. degree (all completed but Ph.D. dissertation). The Ph.D. degree should be obtained before the appointment starts. We are seeking candidates with recent success or strong potential in publishing high-quality and impactful (quantitative and/or qualitative) research in leading management journals. A successful candidate should exhibit a strong willingness and ability to teach courses in organizational behavior and management, as well as a strong willingness and ability to effectively interact with faculty colleagues, students, staff, and external constituents. We are interested in candidates with a grounding in Organizational Behavior or an allied discipline who are pursuing work in the area of Organizational Behavior. Note: Candidates who have not yet conferred their degree will be appointed as an Instructor until the semester following the degree conferral. What We Would Like You to Have Desired qualifications include an established program of research published in leading management journals, or a demonstrated potential in building a strong research pipeline for publications in leading management journals, as well as at least 1 year of experience of teaching organizational behavior and management at the undergraduate, master’s, and/or doctoral levels. Teaching experience can be gained during a candidate’s graduate studies. Teaching duties could include undergraduate/master’s students and doctoral students. Special Instructions To apply, please submit the following materials: Resume/CV Cover Letter Research Statement Teaching Statement Evidence of research effectiveness (e.g., 1–3 journal publications, conference papers, and/or working papers combined into one PDF; If any, at least one submission should be first-authored) Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., student evaluations, course syllabi, and teaching portfolios combined into one PDF) During the application process you will need to enter contact information for three references. We will request letters of recommendation and additional materials, if needed, as the search progresses. Applications received by September 28, 2026 will receive full consideration. Position will remain open until filled. Note: Application materials will not be accepted via email. For consideration, applications must be submitted through CU Boulder Jobs. In compliance with the Colorado Job Application Fairness Act, in any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information. Posting Contact Information Posting Contact Name: Boulder Campus Human Resources Posting Contact Email: Recruiting@colorado.edu Apply Now Share Facebook X Email Help Jobs Submit a Request for Help Frequently Asked Questions For Technical Support: 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) The University of Colorado does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, age, pregnancy, disability, creed, religion, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, veteran status, marital status, political affiliation, or political philosophy. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Click here for a list of ADA and Title IX coordinators . To view the Regent policy , please click here. This organization participates in E-Verify . We will provide the Social Security Administration and, if necessary, the Department of Homeland Security, with information from each employee's I-9 form to confirm work authorization. Reasonable Accommodations for Applicants with Disabilities CU Boulder is committed to making information and resources that are available via the web accessible for all users. If you are a job seeker and need accessibility assistance or an accommodation in order to apply for one of our open positions, please submit an accessibility request or call 303-735-4357 (5-HELP) to submit a request for assistance. Download the Clery Act Annual Security & Fire safety report , or request a paper copy from the CU Boulder Police Department. Administrative and Research Center, East Campus • 3100 Marine St.• Boulder, CO 80309-0565 University of Colorado Boulder © Regents of the University of Colorado Privacy • Legal & Trademarks • Campus Map"
    },
